{
 "_readme": "Genre, form and audience for the books in books-read.md, so the Read tab filters on the same three facets as Candidates. Facts only - the score and the reason live in books-read.md and nothing here may duplicate them. Kept out of books-read.md because that file is hand-maintained prose-plus-table and its parser requires exactly five columns; kept out of book-media.json because that file is regenerable and this is authored.",
 "schema": 1,
 "_key": "slug(title) - the SAME join key as book-media.json's readMedia namespace, computed by the identical slug() in index.html and tools/fetch-media.py. Renaming a title in books-read.md therefore costs a missing facet row, not a broken one, and the Gaps panel reports the orphan rather than hiding the book.",
 "_audience": "Who the edition was published for: adult | ya | childrens. A FACT, not a verdict - how much the children's register actually cost is axis:childrens in book-recommendations.md, and this file is what gives that rule its evidence. Note what the read log now shows on that axis: childrens-audience books run 84 (The Hobbit) and 82 (The Little Prince) down to 51 (Harry Potter), and the low end is low for OCCULT, not for register - so the spread is not a children's penalty.",
 "_form": "novel | novella | stories | nonfiction | verse. `verse` matches the enum tools/promote.py validates against; it exists because Havran 40 ties the lowest score in the log and the reader named the form itself as a cause, which no existing axis covered - short PROSE merely fails to earn points under the short-idea-driven suspension, verse costs.",
